import Lib.Cohomology.Etale.FilteredLimits
import Lib.General.Algebra.CohomologyBaseChange
import Lib.General.Geometry.EtaleCharts

/-!
# p-adic tests: tilts, Fontaine's map, covers by tests and flat base change

A cell is a p-complete, absolutely integrally closed valuation ring in which p is neither zero nor a
unit. A p-adic test c is a non-empty product S = `c.ProdRing` of cells over O_C. Its tilt is
S♭ = `c.TiltRing`. ξ generates the kernel of Fontaine's map θ : W(S♭) → S, and
π = `New.Variety.pFlat` is ξ mod p. The file computes the tilt and the kernel of θ for tests. For
perfect b, it identifies algebra maps b → S♭ with algebra maps O_C ⊗ W(b) → S (`wittFunctor` sends b
to W(b) over A_inf, and `algBaseChange OC` is O_C ⊗_{A_inf} –), so tilting is fully faithful on
tests. It also produces cells over primes and covers by tests, and proves flat base change for
ℤ[Y∘ι], for ι full, faithful and with covering points, when Y is affinely covered.

## Main definitions and results

* `New.Variety.PadicTest.tiltPiEquiv`, `New.Variety.PadicTest.isPerfectTorsionFree_tilt`: S♭ is the
  product of the tilts of the cells; it is perfect and has no π-torsion.
* `New.Variety.PadicTest.ker_theta`: the kernel of Fontaine's θ : W(S♭) → S is generated by ξ.
* `New.Variety.PadicTest.thetaIso`: O_C ⊗_{A_inf} W(S♭) ≅ S, naturally in the test.
* `New.Variety.homTiltIso`: for perfect `b`, algebra maps `b → c.TiltRing` correspond to algebra
  maps `O_C ⊗ W(b) → c.ProdRing` by `f ↦ θ ∘ W(f)`, naturally in the test `c`.
* `New.Variety.hasCoveringPoints_padic`: if an algebra has a point in some test, then all its points
  in tests factor through a single point.
* `New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered.hasFlatBaseChange`, `New.Variety.hasFlatBaseChange_of_iso_reprBy`:
  ℤ[Y∘ι] has flat base change (`New.Variety.HasFlatBaseChange`: its base change maps are bijective
  in all degrees) for affinely covered Y, when ι is full, faithful and has covering points. ℤ[Y] has
  flat base change for Y isomorphic to the points of an O_C-algebra.

Notions from other files:
* `New.OC`: The ring of integers O_C of the field C_p of p-adic complex numbers.
* `New.Variety.PadicTest.algFunctor`: The functor from p-adic tests to commutative O_C-algebras
  sending a test to its product ring S with its structure map; `reprBy B` is the functor of points
  R ↦ (algebra maps B → R), and `Sigma F` is the type of pairs (c, point of `F c`).
* `New.Variety.freeAb`: The functor sending a set-valued functor Y to Z[Y], whose value at A is the
  free abelian group on Y(A).
* `New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered`: `X` is separated and, after restriction along `ι`, covered by one
  affine: there are a `k`-algebra `B` and a point `y` of `X(B)` such that, for every object `c`,
  each point of `X(ι c)` is the image of `y` under some map `B → ι c`.

## Relation to the literature

Known result: Tilting and untilting for products of perfectoid valuation rings over O_C. Only
products of p-complete absolutely integrally closed valuation rings over O_C are treated, and such a
ring is recovered from the Witt vectors of its tilt. Tilting is fully faithful, and maps from a
perfect algebra to the tilt are maps from its untilt. Source: B. Bhatt, M. Morrow, P. Scholze,
Integral p-adic Hodge theory, Publ. Math. IHES 128 (2018), Lemma 3.10; P. Scholze, Perfectoid
spaces, Publ. Math. IHES 116 (2012), Theorem 5.2.

See also `Lib.PadicComparison.Descent.AlmostDescent` and `Lib.Cohomology.Etale.FilteredLimits`.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace New.Variety

/-!
## Tilts of tests and the kernel of Fontaine's map

* `New.Variety.PadicTest.exists_isQuotientByElem`: the quotient of S by an idempotent e ≠ 1 is again
  a test.
-/

section TestProperties

open CategoryTheory TensorProduct Function Ideal Period ConcreteCategory Perfection WittVector
  RingHom

variable {p : ℕ} [ThePrime p] (c : PadicTest)

/-- For ring maps y_i from an O_C-algebra B to a non-empty family of cells W_i, this is the p-adic
test ∏ W_i with structure map O_C → B → ∏ W_i, together with the point (y_i) : B → ∏ W_i. -/
def cellPoint (B : CommAlg OC) {I : Type} [n : Nonempty I] {W : I → Type} [∀ i, CommRing (W i)]
    [∀ i, IsCell p (W i)] (y : ∀ i : I, B.1 →+* W i) :
    Sigma (PadicTest.algFunctor ⋙ reprBy B) where
  fst := { Index := I, Cell := W, structureMap := (RingHom.pi y).comp (algebraMap OC B) }
  snd := ⟨ofHom { toRingHom := RingHom.pi y, commutes' := fun _ ↦ rfl }⟩

namespace PadicTest

/-- The product ring of a p-adic test c is a test ring: reduced, absolutely integrally closed,
and any a, b admit an idempotent e with a ∣ eb and b ∣ (1 − e)a. -/
lemma isTest : IsTest c.ProdRing :=
  IsTest.pi fun _ ↦ isTest_of_preValuationRing

instance : IsAbsIntegrallyClosed c.ProdRing := c.isTest.toIsAbsIntegrallyClosed

/-- Multiplication by `p` is injective on the ring of a p-adic test: each cell is a domain in which
`p ≠ 0`. -/
lemma isLeftRegular_p : IsLeftRegular (p : c.ProdRing) :=
  Pi.isLeftRegular_iff.2 fun i ↦ by simp [isRegular_iff_ne_zero, IsCell.p_ne_zero]

/-- For a p-adic test with cells W_i, the ring isomorphism from the tilt of ∏ W_i to the product
of the tilts W_i^♭ induced by the projections. -/
def tiltPiEquiv :
    Perfection (((i : c.Index) → c.Cell i) ⧸ span {(p : (i : c.Index) → c.Cell i)}) p ≃+*
      ((a : c.Index) → Perfection (c.Cell a ⧸ span {(p : c.Cell a)}) p) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective (RingHom.pi fun i ↦ tiltMap (p := p) (Pi.evalRingHom c.Cell i)) <|
    -- The tilt of a complete ring is the set of its sequences of compatible `p`-th roots
    -- (`quotientMulEquiv`), and such a sequence in a product is a family of such sequences.
    ((quotientMulEquiv ..).bijective_comp _).1 <|
      let split : Perfection (∀ i : c.Index, c.Cell i) p ≃ ∀ i : c.Index, Perfection (c.Cell i) p :=
        ((Equiv.piComm fun _ ↦ c.Cell).subtypeEquiv
            (by simp [funext_iff, forall_comm (α := ℕ)])).trans Equiv.subtypePiEquivPi
      (split.trans (Equiv.piCongrRight fun _ ↦ (quotientMulEquiv ..).1)).bijective

/-- Divisibility in the tilt of a test can be checked after untilting. -/
lemma dvd_of_untilt_dvd {x y : c.TiltRing} (h : x.untilt ∣ y.untilt) : x ∣ y := by
  -- Divisibility is tested in each cell, where it is `untilt_dvd_iff`.
  refine (map_dvd_iff c.tiltPiEquiv).mp (pi_dvd_iff.mpr fun i ↦ untilt_dvd_iff.mp ?_)
  -- The `i`-th component of the tilt of `z` untilts to the `i`-th component of `z.untilt`.
  have h_comp (z : c.TiltRing) : PreTilt.untilt (c.tiltPiEquiv z i) = z.untilt i :=
    untilt_tiltMap (Pi.evalRingHom c.Cell i) z
  simpa [h_comp] using pi_dvd_iff.mp h i

/-- The tilt of a p-adic test c is a perfect O^♭-algebra without `pFlat`-torsion, in the sense of
`New.Variety.IsPerfectTorsionFree`. -/
lemma isPerfectTorsionFree_tilt : IsPerfectTorsionFree (tilt c) := by
  -- If `pFlat • y = 0` then `p * y.untilt = p * (0 : c.TiltRing).untilt`, as the untilt of `pFlat`
  -- divides `p`; cancel `p`.
  change IsPerfectTorsionFree (.of _ c.TiltRing)
  refine ⟨inferInstance, .of_right_eq_zero_of_smul fun y hy ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ : ∃ e : OC, (p : OC) = e * xi.constantCoeff.untilt :=
    exists_eq_mul_left_of_dvd untilt_constantCoeff_xi_dvd_p
  have h_mul (z : c.TiltRing) :
      (p : c.ProdRing) * z.untilt = c.structureMap e * PreTilt.untilt (pFlat • z) := by
    rw [← map_natCast c.structureMap, he, map_mul, ← untilt_tiltMap, mul_assoc, ← map_mul]
    rfl
  have h_untilt : (0 : c.TiltRing).untilt = y.untilt := c.isLeftRegular_p (by simp [h_mul, hy])
  exact zero_dvd_iff.mp (c.dvd_of_untilt_dvd h_untilt.dvd)

/-- Let S be the ring of a p-adic test, that is, the product of its family of valuation rings, with
its ring map from O_C. Then the kernel of Fontaine's map θ: W(S^♭) → S is the principal ideal
generated by the image of ξ = ∑_{0 ≤ i < p} [ε^{1/p}]^i ∈ A_inf = W(O^♭) under the map
W(O^♭) → W(S^♭) induced by the algebra map O^♭ → S^♭, where O^♭ is the tilt of O_C. -/
@[simp]
lemma ker_theta :
    ker (fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p) = span {xi.map (algebraMap OFlat (PreTilt c.ProdRing p))} := by
  -- `θ` kills `ξ`: it commutes with `tiltMap`, and `θ ξ = 0` over `O_C`.
  have hξ : xi.map (algebraMap OFlat c.TiltRing) ∈ ker (fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p) :=
    mem_ker.mpr ((fontaineTheta_map_tiltMap c.structureMap xi).trans (by rw [theta_xi, map_zero]))
  -- A `p`-saturated ideal of Witt vectors is generated by any of its elements whose zeroth
  -- coordinate divides the zeroth coordinates of all its elements
  -- (`Witt.dvd_of_mem_of_constantCoeff_dvd`).
  refine le_antisymm
    (fun w hw ↦ mem_span_singleton.mpr (Witt.dvd_of_mem_of_constantCoeff_dvd hξ ?_ ?_ w hw))
    ((span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).mpr hξ)
  · -- the kernel is `p`-saturated, since `p` is regular in `c.ProdRing`
    simp [c.isLeftRegular_p.mul_left_eq_zero_iff]
  · -- divisibility of zeroth coordinates is read off after untilting: `ξ₀♯ ∣ p ∣ a₀♯`
    refine fun a ha ↦ c.dvd_of_untilt_dvd ?_
    calc
      _ = c.structureMap xi.constantCoeff.untilt := untilt_tiltMap ..
      _ ∣ c.structureMap p := map_dvd _ untilt_constantCoeff_xi_dvd_p
      _ ∣ a.constantCoeff.untilt := by
        -- modulo `p`, `a₀♯` is `θ a = 0`
        simp [← Quotient.eq_zero_iff_dvd, ← mk_fontaineTheta, mem_ker.mp ha]

/-- For an idempotent e ≠ 1 in the ring of a p-adic test c, there is a map of tests f: c → d
that is universal among maps killing e and is the quotient by the ideal (e). -/
lemma exists_isQuotientByElem (e : c.ProdRing) (he : IsIdempotentElem e) (he_ne : e ≠ 1) :
    ∃ (d : PadicTest) (f : c ⟶ d), IsQuotientByElem (B := d) ringFunctor e f := by
  -- project onto the cells where `e i ≠ 1`, that is, where the idempotent `e i` is `0`
  let d := cellPoint (.of OC c.ProdRing) (I := {i // e i ≠ 1})
    (n := nonempty_subtype.mpr (ne_iff.mp he_ne)) fun i ↦ Pi.evalRingHom c.Cell i
  let f : c.ProdRing →ₐ[OC] d.fst.ProdRing := d.snd.down.hom
  have hf_surj : Surjective f := Subtype.surjective_restrict fun i ↦ e i ≠ 1
  have hf_zero : f e = 0 :=
    funext fun i ↦ eq_zero_of_mul_eq_self_left i.property (congrFun he i.val)
  have hf_ker : ker f ≤ span {e} := by
    -- `x ∈ ker f` vanishes on the cells where `e` is not `1`, so `x = x * e`
    refine fun x hx ↦ mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨x, ?_⟩
    have hx_zero (i : c.Index) (hi : e i ≠ 1) : x i = 0 := congrFun hx ⟨i, hi⟩
    simpa [funext_iff, mul_right_eq_self₀, or_iff_not_imp_left] using hx_zero
  refine ⟨d.fst, f, hf_zero, fun d' (g : c.ProdRing →ₐ[OC] d'.ProdRing) hg ↦ ?_, hf_surj, hf_ker⟩
  -- a map `g` that kills `e` kills `ker f`, so factors uniquely through the surjection `f`
  obtain ⟨g₀, h_fac⟩ : ∃ g₀ : d.fst.ProdRing →ₐ[OC] d'.ProdRing, g₀.comp f = g :=
    ⟨_, f.liftOfSurjective_comp hf_surj g (hf_ker.trans ((span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).mpr hg))⟩
  exact ⟨g₀, h_fac, fun g' hg' ↦ (AlgHom.cancel_right hf_surj).mp (hg'.trans h_fac.symm)⟩

/-- The natural isomorphism O_C ⊗_{A_inf} W(S^♭) ≅ S of O_C-algebras on p-adic tests S, induced
by Fontaine's map θ. -/
def thetaIso : tilt ⋙ wittFunctor ⋙ algBaseChange OC ≅ algFunctor :=
  isoOfAppBijective
    ((baseChangeTranspose (tilt ⋙ wittFunctor) algFunctor).invFun
      { app c :=
          ofHom
            { toRingHom := fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p,
              commutes' := fontaineTheta_map_tiltMap c.structureMap }
        naturality _ _ f := ext_apply (fontaineTheta_map_tiltMap f.toRingHom) })
    fun c ↦ by
      constructor
      · -- As `theta` is onto, every element is some `1 ⊗ x`. If `θ x = 0` then `x = ξ • y`
        -- (`ker_theta`), and `1 ⊗ ξ • y = θ ξ • (1 ⊗ y) = 0`.
        refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr
          ((mk_surjective _ _ _ theta_surjective).forall.mpr ?_)
        intro x hx
        obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ : xi.map (algebraMap OFlat (PreTilt c.ProdRing p)) ∣ x :=
          mem_span_singleton.mp (c.ker_theta.le ((one_smul OC _).symm.trans hx))
        -- `erw`: the base change of the Witt functor of the tilt is `OC ⊗ W(c.TiltRing)` only after
        -- unfolding.
        erw [map_smul _ xi, ← algebraMap_smul OC, theta_xi, zero_smul]
        rfl
      · -- θ is onto, as the ring is absolutely integrally closed and p-complete
        intro z
        obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ :=
          fontaineTheta_surjective_of_isAbsIntegrallyClosed (p := p) (R := c.ProdRing) z
        exact ⟨1 ⊗ₜ x, (one_smul OC _).trans hx⟩

/-- The isomorphism `thetaIso` sends `1 ⊗ x` to `θ x`. -/
lemma thetaIso_hom_one_tmul (x : (wittFunctor (WittVector p OFlat)).obj (tilt.obj c)) :
    thetaIso.hom c (1 ⊗ₜ x) = x.fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p :=
  one_smul OC _

end PadicTest

end TestProperties

/-! ## Maps into the tilt and full faithfulness of tilting -/

section TiltAdjunction

open NeZero CategoryTheory Functor Function ConcreteCategory WittVector Perfection PadicTest Period
  CharP

variable {p : ℕ} [ThePrime p]

/-- For a perfect ring `R` of characteristic `p` and a p-adic test `c` (a non-empty family of cells
with a ring map from O_C to their product `c.ProdRing`), ring maps from `R` to the tilt of
`c.ProdRing` correspond bijectively to ring maps `W(R) → c.ProdRing`, by `f ↦ θ ∘ W(f)`, where θ
is Fontaine's map. -/
lemma theta_comp_bijective {R : Type*} {c : PadicTest} [CommRing R] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p] :
    Bijective fun f : R →+* PreTilt c.ProdRing p ↦
      (fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p).comp (WittVector.map f) := by
  constructor
  · -- Modulo `p`, the value at the Teichmüller lift of `x` is the zeroth coordinate of `f x`, and a
    -- map from a perfect ring to the tilt is determined by its zeroth coordinate.
    intro f g h_eq
    refine hom_ext p fun x ↦ ?_
    -- `θ [y]` reduces modulo `p` to the zeroth coordinate of `y`
    show PreTilt.coeff 0 (f x) = PreTilt.coeff 0 (g x)
    simpa using
      congrArg (algebraMap c.ProdRing (ModP c.ProdRing p))
        (RingHom.congr_fun h_eq (teichmuller p x))
  · -- Reduce `g` modulo `p` to a map `g₀` on `R = W(R) / p` and lift `g₀` to the tilt.
    intro g
    let g₀ : R →+* ModP c.ProdRing p := constantCoeff.liftOfRightInverse (teichmuller p) .refl
      ⟨.comp (algebraMap _ _) g, by simp [cast_eq_zero, ker_constantCoeff]⟩
    -- It is enough to compare values at Teichmüller lifts
    -- (`wittVector_ringHom_ext_of_teichmuller`).
    refine ⟨Perfection.lift p R _ g₀, wittVector_ringHom_ext_of_teichmuller fun x ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply]
    -- `Perfection.lift` lands in `Perfection (ModP _) p`, which is `PreTilt` only after unfolding,
    -- so `map_teichmuller` is applied through `congrArg`.
    refine (congrArg (fontaineTheta c.ProdRing p) (map_teichmuller _ _ x)).trans ?_
    -- `θ [y]` is the untilt of `y`, the Teichmüller map of `c.ProdRing`: its value is fixed by
    -- `teichmuller_spec`, as the `n`-th coordinate lifts to `g [x ^ (1 / p ^ n)]`, whose
    -- `p ^ n`-th power is `g [x]`.
    rw [fontaineTheta_teichmuller]
    exact teichmuller_spec fun n ↦ ⟨_, rfl, by simp [← map_pow]⟩

/-- For a perfect algebra `b` over the tilt `OFlat` of `OC`: algebra maps `b → c.TiltRing` over
`OFlat` correspond to algebra maps `OC ⊗ W(b) → c.ProdRing` over `OC` (tensor product over
`W(OFlat)`), naturally in the `p`-adic test `c`. The map `f` goes to the map induced by
`θ ∘ W(f)`. -/
noncomputable def homTiltIso {b : CommAlg OFlat} [PerfectRing b p] :
    tilt ⋙ reprBy b ≅ algFunctor ⋙ reprBy ((wittFunctor ⋙ algBaseChange OC) b) :=
  isoOfAppBijective
    (whiskerLeft tilt
        (pointMap (Y := wittFunctor (WittVector p OFlat) ⋙ algBaseChange OC ⋙ reprBy _) ⟨𝟙 _⟩) ≫
      whiskerRight thetaIso.hom (reprBy _))
    fun c ↦ by
      -- By the adjunction `algBaseChangeAdj` a map from `OC ⊗ W(b)` is an algebra map
      -- `g : W(b) → c.ProdRing`; in these terms the transformation sends `f` to `θ ∘ W(f)`.
      -- `erw`: the points of the base change match the adjunction's hom-set only after unfolding.
      erw [← (Equiv.ulift.trans (algBaseChangeAdj.homEquiv ..)).comp_bijective,
        bijective_iff_existsUnique]
      rintro ⟨g : WittVector p b →+* c.ProdRing, hg⟩
      -- `b` is not zero, as `W(b)` maps to the nonzero `c.ProdRing`, so it has characteristic `p`.
      have h_nontrivial : Nontrivial b :=
        domain_nontrivial (fun x ↦ g (teichmuller p x)) (by simp) (by simp)
      have h_charP : CharP b p := of_ringHom_of_ne_zero (algebraMap OFlat b) p out
      obtain ⟨f, rfl, h_unique⟩ := theta_comp_bijective.existsUnique g
      -- `f` is a map of algebras, since that may be tested after applying `θ ∘ W(–)`.
      have h_alg : f.comp (algebraMap OFlat b) = tiltMap c.structureMap :=
        theta_comp_bijective.injective
          (RingHom.ext fun x ↦ (hg x).trans (fontaineTheta_map_tiltMap c.structureMap x).symm)
      refine ⟨⟨ofHom ⟨f, (f.comp _).congr_fun h_alg⟩⟩, ?_, fun ⟨f'⟩ hf' ↦ ?_⟩
      · exact ext_apply fun _ ↦ c.thetaIso_hom_one_tmul _
      · -- `f'` and `f` have the same image under `θ ∘ W(–)`, read off from `hf'` at `1 ⊗ x`.
        have h_eq : f'.hom.toRingHom = f := h_unique _ <| RingHom.ext fun x ↦
          (c.thetaIso_hom_one_tmul _).symm.trans (congrArg (fun φ ↦ φ.hom x) hf')
        exact congrArg _ (ext_apply (RingHom.congr_fun h_eq))

/-- Tilting is full: every map between the tilts of two tests is the tilt of a map of tests. -/
instance : tilt.Full where
  map_surjective {X Y} f := by
    -- Conjugating `OC ⊗ W(f)` by `thetaIso` gives a map `g` of tests. By naturality `tilt.map g`
    -- and `f` have the same image under the bijection `homTiltIso`.
    let g : X ⟶ Y :=
      (thetaIso.inv.app X ≫ (wittFunctor ⋙ algBaseChange _).map f ≫ thetaIso.hom.app Y).hom
    have h_same_image :
        (wittFunctor ⋙ algBaseChange OC).map (tilt.map g) ≫ thetaIso.hom.app Y =
          (wittFunctor ⋙ algBaseChange OC).map f ≫ thetaIso.hom.app Y :=
      (thetaIso.hom.naturality g).trans (thetaIso.hom_inv_id_app_assoc ..)
    exact ⟨g, congrArg ULift.down <| (homTiltIso (b := .of OFlat (PreTilt X.ProdRing p))).app Y
      |>.toEquiv.injective (congrArg ULift.up h_same_image)⟩

instance : algFunctor.Faithful := ⟨congrArg hom⟩

instance : tilt.Faithful := .of_comp_iso thetaIso

end TiltAdjunction

/-!
## Cells over primes, covers by tests and flat base change

* `New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered.devissage_bijective`: dévissage from representable to affinely
  covered functors.
-/

section TestCover

open CategoryTheory Ideal ValuationRing Pi Filter Germ Envelope Quot Adic IsLocalization Function
  HasBaseChange PadicTest

variable {p : ℕ}

/-- An ultrapower of a ring in which divisibility is total, along the hyperfilter on `ℕ`, is again
such a ring (`PreValuationRing`): of two germs, one divides the other at almost all indices. -/
lemma preValuationRing_hyperfilter_germ {R : Type} [CommRing R] [PreValuationRing R] :
    PreValuationRing ((hyperfilter ℕ).Germ R) := by
  let γ : (ℕ → R) →+* (hyperfilter ℕ).Germ R := coeRingHom _
  have hγ : Surjective γ := exists_rep
  refine ⟨hγ.forall₂.mpr fun a b ↦ ?_⟩
  choose c hc using fun n ↦ cond (a n) (b n)
  have h_ae : (∀ᶠ n in hyperfilter ℕ, a n * c n = b n) ∨ ∀ᶠ n in hyperfilter ℕ, b n * c n = a n :=
    Ultrafilter.eventually_or.mp (Filter.Eventually.of_forall hc)
  exact ⟨γ c, h_ae.imp sound sound⟩

/-- In an ultrapower along the hyperfilter on `ℕ`, every system `x j - a * x (j + 1) = c j` is
solvable (`shiftDiff`), for a natural number `a`. -/
lemma surjective_shiftDiff_hyperfilter_germ {R : Type} [CommRing R] (a : ℕ) :
    Surjective (shiftDiff ((hyperfilter ℕ).Germ R) (a : (hyperfilter ℕ).Germ R)) := by
  let γ : (ℕ → R) →+* (hyperfilter ℕ).Germ R := coeRingHom _
  have hγ : Surjective γ := exists_rep
  refine hγ.comp_left.forall.mpr fun c ↦ ?_
  -- At index `k`, the finite sum `c j + a * c (j + 1) + ⋯ + a ^ (k - 1 - j) * c (k - 1)` solves
  -- the equations with `j < k`.
  let x : ℕ → ℕ → R := fun j k ↦ (List.Ico j k).foldr (fun i z ↦ c i k + a * z) 0
  refine ⟨fun j ↦ γ (x j), funext fun j ↦ sound (Nat.hyperfilter_le_atTop ?_)⟩
  exact (eventually_gt_atTop j).mono fun k hk ↦ by simp [x, List.Ico.eq_cons hk]

/-! ### Cells and universal covers -/

/-- If B is p-torsion-free and m is a prime ideal of B containing p, there are a cell W
(`New.Variety.IsCell`) and a ring map B → W sending every element of m to a non-unit. -/
lemma exists_cell_over {B : Type} [CommRing.{0} B] {m : Ideal B} (hm_prime : IsPrime m)
    (hp_reg : IsSMulRegular B p) (hp : ↑p ∈ m) :
    ∃ W : Type, ∃ (_ : CommRing W) (_ : IsCell p W) (y : B →+* W), ∀ z ∈ m, ¬IsUnit (y z) := by
  -- Take an absolutely integrally closed valuation ring `U` with centre `m` in which `p ≠ 0`, and
  -- its ultrapower `G`. Then `G` maps onto its `p`-adic completion `W`, which is the cell.
  let L : Type := Localization.AtPrime m
  let K : Type :=
    AlgebraicClosure (Classical.arbitrary (PrimeSpectrum (FractionRing L))).asIdeal.ResidueField
  -- `K` is an algebraically closed field with a map from `FractionRing L`, and `U ⊆ K` a
  -- valuation subring that receives `L` by a local map
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hU_local⟩ : ∃ (U : ValuationSubring K) (hU : ∀ x, algebraMap L K x ∈ U.toSubring),
      IsLocalHom ((algebraMap L K).codRestrict U.toSubring hU) :=
    IsLocalRing.exists_factor_valuationRing _
  let G : Type := (hyperfilter ℕ).Germ U
  let γ : (ℕ → U) →+* G := coeRingHom _
  have hγ : Surjective γ := exists_rep
  let φ : B →+* G := γ.comp (.pi fun _ ↦ .comp (.codRestrict _ U.toSubring hU) (algebraMap B L))
  -- An inverse of `φ z` in `G` gives an inverse in `U` at some index, and `L → U` is local.
  have hφ (z : B) (hz : z ∈ m) : ¬φ z ∣ 1 := by
    intro h_dvd
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hγ.exists.mp h_dvd
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (coe_eq.mp hw).exists
    have h_unit : IsUnit ((algebraMap L K).codRestrict U.toSubring hU (algebraMap B L z)) :=
      isUnit_of_dvd_one ⟨w n, hn⟩
    exact (AtPrime.isUnit_to_map_iff L m z).mp (hU_local.map_nonunit _ h_unit) hz
  have hG_val : PreValuationRing G := preValuationRing_hyperfilter_germ
  have h_precomplete : IsPrecomplete (span {(p : G)}) G := by
    simpa using isPrecomplete_of_shiftDiff_surjective (surjective_shiftDiff_hyperfilter_germ p)
      (surjective_shiftDiff_hyperfilter_germ p)
  let W : Type := PrincipalCompletion G p
  let π : G →+* W := algebraMap G W
  have hπ : Surjective π := AdicCompletion.of_surjective_iff.mpr h_precomplete
  -- `p` is regular in `B`, so also in `L`; hence it is a unit in `FractionRing L` and in `K`.
  have hp_mem : (p : B) ∈ nonZeroDivisors B := mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mpr fun x hx ↦
    hp_reg.right_eq_zero_of_smul (by simpa using hx)
  have hp_nzd : algebraMap B L p ∈ nonZeroDivisors L :=
    map_nonZeroDivisors_le m.primeCompl L ⟨p, hp_mem, rfl⟩
  have hp_unit : IsUnit (p : K) := by
    simpa using (map_units (FractionRing L) ⟨_, hp_nzd⟩).map (algebraMap _ K)
  have hG_reg : IsSMulRegular G p := by
    refine hγ.forall₂.mpr fun a b hab ↦ sound ((coe_eq.mp hab).mono fun n hn ↦ ?_)
    -- In `K`, cancel the unit `p`.
    exact Subtype.ext (hp_unit.mul_left_cancel (by simpa using congrArg Subtype.val hn))
  have h_reg : IsSMulRegular W p := isSMulRegular_completion (R := G) hG_reg
  -- `W` is nontrivial: `π p = 1` would make `φ p` divide `1`.
  have hW_nontrivial : Nontrivial W :=
    nontrivial_of_ne (π p ^ 1) (π 1) fun h_eq ↦ hφ p hp (by simpa using pow_dvd_iff.mp h_eq.dvd)
  have hW_val : PreValuationRing W := hπ.preValuationRing π.toMulHom
  -- Let `a * b = 0`, `b ≠ 0`. If `a ∣ p ^ n` then `p ^ n * b = 0`, which is impossible; so all
  -- powers of `p` divide `a`, and `a = 0` in the completion.
  have hW_nzd : NoZeroDivisors W := by
    refine ⟨fun {a b} hab ↦ or_iff_not_imp_right.mpr fun hb ↦ eq_zero_of_forall_pow_dvd fun n ↦ ?_⟩
    refine (dvd_total _ a).resolve_right ?_
    rintro ⟨d, hd⟩
    refine hb (h_reg.pow n ?_)
    have h_pow : (p : W) ^ n = a * d := by rwa [← map_natCast π]
    simp [h_pow, mul_right_comm, hab]
  have hW_domain : IsDomain W := NoZeroDivisors.to_isDomain W
  -- `U` is absolutely integrally closed as `K` is; so are `ℕ → U` and its quotients
  have h_test : IsTest (ℕ → U) := IsTest.pi fun _ ↦ isTest_of_preValuationRing
  have h_cell : IsCell p W :=
    { toIsAdicComplete := isAdicComplete
      toIsAbsIntegrallyClosed := (h_test.of_surjective hγ).of_surjective hπ
      p_ne_zero := by simpa using h_reg.ne one_ne_zero }
  -- the elements of `m` go to non-units, as `π` is local
  exact ⟨W, inferInstance, h_cell, π.comp φ,
    fun z hz hu ↦ hφ z hz (hπ.isLocalHom.map_nonunit _ hu).dvd⟩

/-- A subring `g : W → V` of a cell is again a cell if every equation `IsSolution` with coefficients
in `W` that is solvable in `V` is solvable in `W` (`New.Variety.Envelope.IsSolutionClosed`). -/
lemma isCell_of_isSolutionClosed {W V : Type} [CommRing W] [CommRing V] {g : W →+* V}
    (hg : Envelope.IsSolutionClosed g) [hV : IsCell p V] :
    IsCell p W := by
  -- `g` is injective and reflects divisibility, so most properties are read off in `V`. The `↓`
  -- lets `smodEq_span_pow_iff_dvd` rewrite before `simp` unfolds the `SMOD` relation.
  have hW_domain : IsDomain W := hg.1.isDomain
  have hW_val : ValuationRing W := iff_dvd_total.mpr ⟨by simp [← hg.map_dvd_iff, dvd_total]⟩
  refine
    { haus' := by simp_all [← hg.1.eq_iff, ← hg.map_dvd_iff, hV.haus, ↓ smodEq_span_pow_iff_dvd]
      prec' f hf := ?_
      toIsAbsIntegrallyClosed := (hg.isTest isTest_of_preValuationRing).toIsAbsIntegrallyClosed
      p_ne_zero := by simp [← hg.1.eq_iff, hV.p_ne_zero] }
  -- `g ∘ f` is again Cauchy in `V`, as `g` reflects divisibility.
  have h_cauchy {m n : ℕ} (h_le : m ≤ n) :
      g (f m) ≡ g (f n) [SMOD (span {(p : V)} ^ m • ⊤ : Submodule V V)] := by
    simp_all [← hg.map_dvd_iff, ↓ smodEq_span_pow_iff_dvd]
  -- the limit is a solution of equation `1`, `∀ n, a 0 ^ n ∣ a (n + 1) - x`, with coefficients
  -- `a = p, f 0, f 1, …`
  let a : ℕ → W := fun n ↦ n.casesOn (p : W) f
  have h_lim : ∃ x : V, IsSolution (g ∘ a) x 1 := by
    simpa [a, IsSolution, ↓ smodEq_span_pow_iff_dvd] using hV.prec' (g ∘ f) h_cauchy
  -- the solution `x` in `W` is the limit: `p ^ n ∣ f n - x` for every `n`, read back along `g`
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hg.2 1 a h_lim
  exact ⟨x, by simpa [a, IsSolution, ← hg.map_dvd_iff, ↓ smodEq_span_pow_iff_dvd] using hx⟩

variable [ThePrime p]

/-- Universal cover by a test: `New.Variety.PadicTest.algFunctor` has covering points
(`New.Variety.HasCoveringPoints`). If the O_C-algebra B has a point (an O_C-algebra map to the ring
of the test) in some p-adic test, then there are a test c and a point y of B in c through which
every point of B in any test d factors by a map of tests c → d. -/
instance hasCoveringPoints_padic : HasCoveringPoints algFunctor :=
  .mk fun B c z₀ ↦ by
    -- Every map from `B` to a cell factors through a cell that is a quotient of one fixed
    -- polynomial ring over `B`. The product of all such quotients is the covering test. `φ d z j`
    -- extends the `j`-th component of the point `z` to the polynomial ring (`hφ`), and its image
    -- holds solutions of all equations solvable in the cell (`hφ_clo`)
    have h_ext (d : PadicTest) (z : B →+* PadicTest.ProdRing d) (j : d.Index) :
        ∃ g : MvPolynomial (SolutionName B) B →+* d.Cell j,
          g.comp MvPolynomial.C = (evalRingHom d.Cell j).comp z ∧ IsSolutionClosed g.kerLift :=
      exists_isSolutionClosed ((evalRingHom d.Cell j).comp z)
    choose φ hφ hφ_clo using h_ext
    let Idx : Type := {q : Ideal (MvPolynomial (SolutionName B) B) // IsCell p (_ ⧸ q)}
    let idx (d : PadicTest) (z : B →+* d.ProdRing) (j : d.Index) : Idx :=
      ⟨RingHom.ker (φ d z j), isCell_of_isSolutionClosed (hφ_clo d z j) (hV := d.isCell j)⟩
    have h_cell (q : Idx) : IsCell p (MvPolynomial (SolutionName B) B ⧸ q.val) := q.property
    let y := cellPoint B (n := ⟨idx c z₀.down.hom.toRingHom c.nonempty.some⟩)
      fun q : Idx ↦ algebraMap B (_ ⧸ q.val)
    refine ⟨y.fst, y.snd, fun d z ↦ ?_⟩
    -- the map to the `j`-th cell of `d`: project to the quotient by `ker (φ d z j)`, then embed
    let ψ : y.fst.ProdRing →+* d.ProdRing :=
      .pi fun j ↦ (φ d z.down.hom.toRingHom j).kerLift.comp
        (evalRingHom (fun q : Idx ↦ _ ⧸ q.val) (idx d z.down.hom.toRingHom j))
    have hψ (x : B) : ψ (y.snd.down.hom x) = z.down.hom x :=
      funext fun j ↦ RingHom.congr_fun (hφ d z.down.hom.toRingHom j) x
    exact ⟨⟨⟨ψ, fun a ↦ (hψ _).trans (z.down.hom.commutes a)⟩⟩,
      congrArg ULift.up (ConcreteCategory.ext_apply hψ)⟩

/-- The functor `New.Variety.PadicTest.algFunctor` is full: maps of tests are by definition the
`O_C`-algebra maps between their product rings. -/
instance : algFunctor.Full := ⟨by tauto⟩

variable {C : Type _} [Category C] {A : Type} [CommRing A] {ι : C ⥤ CommAlg A}

/-! ### Flat base change for affinely covered functors -/

/-- Flat base change (`New.Variety.HasFlatBaseChange`) defines a closed class of functors from C to
abelian groups: it contains 0, and for M' ⊂ M with M' in the class, M is in it exactly when M/M'
is. -/
lemma HasFlatBaseChange.isClosedClass : IsClosedClass (D := C) HasFlatBaseChange := by
  simp_all [IsClosedClass, HasFlatBaseChange, AllBijective, devissage.isClosedClass.1,
    devissage.isClosedClass.2]

/-- The functor of points of an A-algebra B in the algebras ι(c) is affinely covered. -/
lemma isAffinelyCovered_reprBy (B : CommAlg A) : IsAffinelyCovered ι (reprBy B) := by
  refine ⟨⟨fun R x y ↦ ?_⟩, B, ⟨𝟙 B⟩, by tauto⟩
  -- a map equalises two points `x y : B ⟶ R` if and only if it kills all differences `x a - y a`
  refine ⟨⨆ a, span {x.down.hom a - y.down.hom a}, fun _ _ ↦ ULift.up_inj.trans ?_⟩
  simp [ConcreteCategory.hom_ext_iff, sub_eq_zero]

variable [ι.Full] [ι.Faithful] [HasCoveringPoints ι] {Y : CommAlg A ⥤ Type 1}

open Limits CommAlgCat Quotient Subfunctor ShortComplex

omit [ι.Full] [ι.Faithful] [HasCoveringPoints ι] in
/-- Let `ι` be any functor from `C` to `A`-algebras, and let `X` be a separated functor on
`A`-algebras, meaning that for any two points of X(B) there is an ideal J of B such that a map φ :
B → B' makes them equal exactly when φ kills J. Let `y` be a point of `X` over `B` and `η : B ⟶ T`.
Then the fibre powers (`New.Variety.cech`, `m + 1` factors) of the composite h_T → h_B → X, given by
`η` and `y`, are affinely covered relative to `ι`: each is separated and has a single point over
some `A`-algebra from which every point over every `ι c` is obtained by some map
(`New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered`). -/
lemma isAffinelyCovered_cech {X : CommAlg A ⥤ Type 1} (hX : IsSeparatedFunctor X) {T B : CommAlg A}
    (η : B ⟶ T) (y : X.obj B) (m : ℕ) :
    IsAffinelyCovered ι (cech (reprMap η ≫ pointMap y) m) := by
  constructor
  · -- two tuples agree exactly where the differences of their coordinates vanish
    refine ⟨fun _ x x' ↦ ⟨⨆ (i) (a), span {(x.val i).down.hom a - (x'.val i).down.hom a}, ?_⟩⟩
    simp +instances [cech, funext_iff, reprFunctor, ConcreteCategory.hom_ext_iff, sub_eq_zero]
  -- On the tensor power of `T`, with coprojections `e i`, the images of `y` along `e i` and `e j`
  -- become equal exactly when an ideal `J i j` is killed, because `X` is separated.
  let e : Fin (m + 1) → (T ⟶ ∐ fun _ ↦ T) := Sigma.ι fun _ ↦ T
  choose J hJ_raw using fun i j ↦ hX.exists_ideal _ (X.map (η ≫ e i) y) (X.map (η ≫ e j) y)
  have hJ : ∀ (i j : Fin (m + 1)) (B' : CommAlg A) (φ : (∐ fun _ ↦ T) ⟶ B'),
      X.map (η ≫ Sigma.ι (fun _ ↦ T) i ≫ φ) y = X.map (η ≫ Sigma.ι (fun _ ↦ T) j ≫ φ) y ↔
        J i j ≤ RingHom.ker φ.hom := by
    simpa [e, ← X.map_comp_apply, -Functor.map_comp] using hJ_raw
  -- so the universal tuple over the quotient by all `J i j` lies in the fibre power
  let π : (∐ fun _ : Fin (m + 1) ↦ T) ⟶ of A ((↑(∐ fun _ ↦ T) : Type) ⧸ iSup (uncurry J)) :=
    ofHom (mkₐ A (iSup J.uncurry))
  refine ⟨_, ⟨fun i ↦ ⟨e i ≫ π⟩, fun i j ↦ ?_⟩, fun d x ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact (hJ i j _ π).mpr ((le_iSup J.uncurry (i, j)).trans mk_ker.ge)
  -- and every point `x` of the fibre power kills all `J i j`, so it factors through the quotient
  let σ : (∐ fun _ ↦ T) ⟶ ι.obj d := Limits.Sigma.desc fun i : Fin (m + 1) ↦ (x.val i).down
  have h_agree (i j : Fin (m + 1)) :
      X.map (η ≫ Sigma.ι (fun _ ↦ T) i ≫ σ) y = X.map (η ≫ Sigma.ι (fun _ ↦ T) j ≫ σ) y := by
    -- `using!`: the maps `pointMap y` and `reprMap η` unfold to `X.map` only by definition.
    simpa [σ, -Functor.map_comp] using! x.prop i j
  have h_kill : iSup J.uncurry ≤ RingHom.ker σ.hom :=
    iSup_le fun ⟨i, j⟩ ↦ (hJ i j (ι.obj d) σ).mp (h_agree i j)
  -- coordinate `i` of the factored tuple is `Sigma.ι i ≫ σ`, which is `x.val i`
  exact ⟨⟨ofHom (liftₐ _ _ h_kill)⟩, Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦
    congrArg ULift.up (Sigma.ι_comp_desc (fun i ↦ (x.val i).down) i)⟩

/-- Let ι from C to A-algebras be fully faithful, and suppose that each A-algebra B with a point in
some ι(c) has one point through which all its points factor (`New.Variety.HasCoveringPoints`). Let
`f` be a family of maps `M N' n → N N' n`, indexed by functors `N'` from C to abelian groups and
degrees n. Suppose it satisfies the five and four lemmas like a map of contravariant δ-functors
(`New.Variety.Devissage`). If f is bijective in all degrees at ℤ[h_c] for every object c of C, then
it is so at ℤ[Y∘ι] for every affinely covered Y. Here Y is separated and has one point y ∈ Y(B) of
which every point of each Y(ι c) is an image (`New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered`). -/
lemma IsAffinelyCovered.devissage_bijective {M N : C ⥤ Ab → ℕ → Type _}
    {f : (N' : C ⥤ Ab) → (n : ℕ) → M N' n → N N' n} (h : Devissage (D := C) (A := M) (B := N) f)
    (h_rep : ∀ c : C, AllBijective (f (freeAb.obj (reprBy c)))) (hY : IsAffinelyCovered ι Y) :
    AllBijective (f (freeAb.obj (ι ⋙ Y))) := by
  -- Induction on the number `r` of conditions in `BijectiveUpTo`, for all affinely covered `Y`.
  refine allBijective_iff_forall_bijectiveUpTo.mpr fun r ↦ ?_
  induction r generalizing Y with
  | zero => simp [BijectiveUpTo]
  | succ r ih =>
    obtain ⟨d, ⟨w⟩⟩ | h_empty := em (∃ d, Nonempty ((ι ⋙ Y).obj d))
    swap
    · -- without points, `freeAb.obj (ι ⋙ Y)` is zero
      have h_id_zero : 𝟙 (freeAb.obj (ι ⋙ Y)) = 0 :=
        freeAb.hom_ext fun d w ↦ (h_empty ⟨d, ⟨w⟩⟩).elim
      exact allBijective_iff_forall_bijectiveUpTo.mp (h.isClosedClass.1 _ h_id_zero) _
    -- cover `ι ⋙ Y` by a representable functor
    obtain ⟨hY_sep, B, y, hy⟩ := hY
    obtain ⟨c, ⟨η⟩, hη⟩ := HasCoveringPoints.exists_surjective_point B (hy d w).choose
    let q := reprMap η ≫ pointMap y
    let Q : Subfunctor (ι ⋙ Y) := range (ι.whiskerLeft q)
    -- the image `Q` is all of `ι ⋙ Y`, as every point of `Y` comes from `y` and `η`
    have h_iso : IsIso Q.ι := by
      refine Q.eq_top_iff_isIso.mp (top_unique fun d x _ ↦ ?_)
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (hy d).comp (hη d) x
      exact ⟨⟨ι.map a.down⟩, ha⟩
    -- Čech descent: `r + 1` conditions on the cover and `r` on its fibre powers give `r + 1` on the
    -- image, which is all of `ι ⋙ Y`
    have h_cover : AllBijective (f (freeAb.obj (ι ⋙ reprBy (ι.obj c)))) :=
      h.isClosedClass.freeAb_of_bijective _ (pointMap_id_bijective_of_fullyFaithful ι c) (h_rep c)
    have h_range : BijectiveUpTo (f (freeAb.obj Q.toFunctor)) (r + 1) :=
      cech_descent_step _ h.toStepwiseFourLemma (allBijective_iff_forall_bijectiveUpTo.mp h_cover _)
        fun m ↦ ih (isAffinelyCovered_cech hY_sep η y m)
    -- pass along the isomorphism from the image, whose kernel is zero
    have h_ker : AllBijective (f (kernel (freeAb.map Q.ι))) :=
      h.isClosedClass.1 _ ((isZero_kernel_of_mono _).eq_of_src _ _)
    exact h.bijectiveUpTo_quotient ⟨exact_kernel (freeAb.map Q.ι)⟩ h_range
      (allBijective_iff_forall_bijectiveUpTo.mp h_ker _)

/-- Let ι from C to A-algebras be fully faithful, and suppose each A-algebra B with a point in some
ι(c) has one point through which all its points factor (`New.Variety.HasCoveringPoints`). If Y is
affinely covered (`New.Variety.IsAffinelyCovered`), then ℤ[Y∘ι] has flat base change. -/
lemma IsAffinelyCovered.hasFlatBaseChange (hY : IsAffinelyCovered ι Y) :
    HasFlatBaseChange (freeAb (ι ⋙ Y)) := by
  simp_all [HasFlatBaseChange, devissage_bijective devissage
    HasBaseChange.baseChangeMap_bijective_freeAb_reprBy]

/-- If a functor Y on p-adic tests is isomorphic to the points of an O_C-algebra B, then ℤ[Y] has
flat base change. -/
lemma hasFlatBaseChange_of_iso_reprBy {B : CommAlg OC} {Y : PadicTest ⥤ Type 1}
    (e : algFunctor ⋙ reprBy B ≅ Y) :
    HasFlatBaseChange (freeAb Y) :=
  (HasFlatBaseChange.isClosedClass.iff_of_isIso (freeAb.map e.hom)).mp
    (isAffinelyCovered_reprBy B).hasFlatBaseChange

end TestCover

